    "learning_objective": "Understand every step of finding this limit, and why each step is allowed.",
    "teaching_message": "Here is the full solution, step by step. The limit is 6. Ask me about any step you want me to explain.",
    "visible_board_actions": [
      {
        "id": "ws-step-read-0",
        "type": "write_text",
        "sequence_index": 0,
        "duration_ms": 450,
        "section_id": "step-read",
        "layout_zone": "working",
        "layout_flow": "vertical",
        "text": "Step 1 · Understand the question. We want to know what value f(x) gets closer and closer to as x gets closer to 3. x does not have to equal 3 — we look at values near it.",
        "problem_instance_id": "problem-ad8bae3e315c4a07beec9325d03b55de",
        "active_step_id": "lesson-problem-ad8bae3e315c4a07beec9325d03b55de:step-0:ws-next-14",
        "board_version": 1,
        "base_board_version": 0,
        "action_id": "ws-step-read-0"
      },
      {
        "id": "ws-step-read-1",
        "type": "write_equation",
        "sequence_index": 1,
        "duration_ms": 550,
        "section_id": "step-read",
        "layout_zone": "working",
        "layout_flow": "vertical",
        "latex": "\\lim_{x \\to 3} \\frac{x^{2} - 9}{x - 3}",
        "problem_instance_id": "problem-ad8bae3e315c4a07beec9325d03b55de",
        "active_step_id": "lesson-problem-ad8bae3e315c4a07beec9325d03b55de:step-0:ws-next-14",
        "board_version": 1,
        "base_board_version": 0,
        "action_id": "ws-step-read-1"
      },
      {
        "id": "ws-step-try-2",
        "type": "write_text",
        "sequence_index": 2,
        "duration_ms": 450,
        "section_id": "step-try",
        "layout_zone": "working",
        "layout_flow": "vertical",
        "text": "Step 2 · Try substituting first. Putting x = 3 in gives 0/0. This is called an indeterminate form. It does not mean the answer is 0 — it tells us to simplify the expression before substituting.",
        "problem_instance_id": "problem-ad8bae3e315c4a07beec9325d03b55de",
        "active_step_id": "lesson-problem-ad8bae3e315c4a07beec9325d03b55de:step-0:ws-next-14",
        "board_version": 1,
        "base_board_version": 0,
        "action_id": "ws-step-try-2"
      },
      {
        "id": "ws-step-try-3",
        "type": "write_equation",
        "sequence_index": 3,
        "duration_ms": 550,
        "section_id": "step-try",
        "layout_zone": "working",
        "layout_flow": "vertical",
        "latex": "\\frac{3^{2} - 9}{3 - 3} = \\frac{0}{0}",
        "problem_instance_id": "problem-ad8bae3e315c4a07beec9325d03b55de",
        "active_step_id": "lesson-problem-ad8bae3e315c4a07beec9325d03b55de:step-0:ws-next-14",
        "board_version": 1,
        "base_board_version": 0,
        "action_id": "ws-step-try-3"
      },
      {
        "id": "ws-step-factor-4",
        "type": "write_text",
        "sequence_index": 4,
        "duration_ms": 450,
        "section_id": "step-factor",
        "layout_zone": "working",
        "layout_flow": "vertical",
        "text": "Step 3 · Factor the top and bottom. x² − 9 is a difference of squares: a² − b² = (a − b)(a + b). Both parts share the factor (x − 3), which is exactly what makes 0/0.",
        "problem_instance_id": "problem-ad8bae3e315c4a07beec9325d03b55de",
        "active_step_id": "lesson-problem-ad8bae3e315c4a07beec9325d03b55de:step-0:ws-next-14",
        "board_version": 1,
        "base_board_version": 0,
        "action_id": "ws-step-factor-4"
      },
      {
        "id": "ws-step-factor-5",
        "type": "write_equation",
        "sequence_index": 5,
        "duration_ms": 550,
        "section_id": "step-factor",
        "layout_zone": "working",
        "layout_flow": "vertical",
        "latex": "\\frac{x^{2} - 9}{x - 3} = \\frac{\\left(x - 3\\right) \\left(x + 3\\right)}{x - 3}",
        "problem_instance_id": "problem-ad8bae3e315c4a07beec9325d03b55de",
        "active_step_id": "lesson-problem-ad8bae3e315c4a07beec9325d03b55de:step-0:ws-next-14",
        "board_version": 1,
        "base_board_version": 0,
        "action_id": "ws-step-factor-5"
      },
      {
        "id": "ws-step-cancel-6",
        "type": "write_text",
        "sequence_index": 6,
        "duration_ms": 450,
        "section_id": "step-cancel",
        "layout_zone": "working",
        "layout_flow": "vertical",
        "text": "Step 4 · Cancel the common factor. We can cancel (x − 3) because x only gets close to 3 and never equals it, so (x − 3) is never zero.",
        "problem_instance_id": "problem-ad8bae3e315c4a07beec9325d03b55de",
        "active_step_id": "lesson-problem-ad8bae3e315c4a07beec9325d03b55de:step-0:ws-next-14",
        "board_version": 1,
        "base_board_version": 0,
        "action_id": "ws-step-cancel-6"
      },
      {
        "id": "ws-step-cancel-7",
        "type": "write_equation",
        "sequence_index": 7,
        "duration_ms": 550,
        "section_id": "step-cancel",
        "layout_zone": "working",
        "layout_flow": "vertical",
        "latex": "\\frac{x^{2} - 9}{x - 3} = x + 3, \\quad x \\neq 3",
        "problem_instance_id": "problem-ad8bae3e315c4a07beec9325d03b55de",
        "active_step_id": "lesson-problem-ad8bae3e315c4a07beec9325d03b55de:step-0:ws-next-14",
        "board_version": 1,
        "base_board_version": 0,
        "action_id": "ws-step-cancel-7"
      },
      {
